From 507c7768e1f10de76d3599d8b642a1c36af59ea3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 20:46:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09106/11362] Surface the quarantine the gate was reading past:
 the .539 answer was already on disk

Extends REQ-OPS-GATE-NULL-DIAGNOSTIC-6266, from tracing the four .539 blocks to
their actual cause rather than stopping at the null field.

exp6228 recorded `status: preconditions_recorded`, `duration_s: 0.0`, and
`flagged_adversarial: true` with a CRITICAL NONTERMINAL_DECLARED_ARTIFACT
corrigendum. The task checked its preconditions and never ran the experiment. The
seven `.token` files beside it are 4 bytes each, so there is no measurement to
recover. adversarial_verify.py caught all of this and stamped the artifact.

Then four gates read that same file and reported `actual=None == expected=1`,
never mentioning the stamp sitting beside the field they were reading. The system
knew. Nothing connected the fabrication gate to the pre-gate, so the diagnosis was
on disk for ten milestones with nobody looking at it.

The quarantine check now runs FIRST, ahead of the null-versus-absent split
committed a moment ago, because it changes the instruction rather than refining
it. "The field is null, fill it in" is wrong advice for an artifact the
fabrication gate has already rejected. The message names the corrigendum kind and
the status, says the upstream has to actually run, and repeats the CLAUDE.md rule
that a flagged artifact's numbers are never aggregated.

Verified against the real artifact, not a fixture. Test proven to bite by
mutation: removing the branch turns it red.

NOT DOING, and stating it because the temptation is real: exp6228's artifact is
not being backfilled. It is the honest record of a run that stopped at
preconditions. Writing values into it now would be me deciding what the run
concluded, which is the fabrication this project spends most of its guard budget
preventing. The four tasks it blocked were superseded -- the three-family lane
continued through exp6300, 6303, 6314, 6317, 6327 and 6380 -- so nothing is
blocked today.

